    <shape type="text" topLeftX="600" topLeftY="194" width="300" height="180">
      <content textType="body" fontSize="13" fontFamily="Inter" color="rgba(51,65,92,1)" lineSpacing="multiple:1.5">
        <p>Content keeps a comfortable reading width on large screens.</p>
        <p>Side margins grow with the viewport, so the page never looks stretched.</p>
        <p>Matches the desktop-first design of our sample page.</p>
      </content>
    </shape>
  </data>
  <note>
    <content textType="body">
      <p>For the page layout we chose the jello layout, as required by the assignment.</p>
      <p>In a jello layout, the content area has a fixed maximum width and is centered, while the margins on both sides expand and contract with the screen size.</p>
      <p>We implemented this with a maximum width of 900 pixels and margin auto centering, which keeps text readable and consistent across screen sizes.</p>
    </content>
  </note>
